railwatch-server bundles the Railwatch server.

The platform gems of railwatch-server (x86_64-linux, aarch64-linux,
x86_64-darwin, arm64-darwin) contain exe/<platform>/railwatch, a compiled
build of Railwatch (railwatch-rs), https://github.com/Rebulk/railwatch-rs,
which is free software under the GNU Affero General Public License,
version 3 only (AGPL-3.0-only). This gem's own Ruby code is under the same
license; see LICENSE.

The Corresponding Source of the bundled binary is the railwatch-rs commit
named in lib/railwatch/server/version.rb (RAILWATCH_RS), unmodified. The
running server also links to its source on every response (the Link header and /source).
Third-party code compiled into the binary keeps its own licenses, listed in
railwatch-rs's THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.

Running this gem in your application does not make your application a
derivative of Railwatch: the server is a separate program, started as its
own process and spoken to over HTTP. If you modify the server and offer it
to users over a network, AGPL-3.0 section 13 asks you to offer them the
source of your version.

The railwatch gem (https://github.com/Rebulk/railwatch), the agent that
reports your app's telemetry, is a separate gem under the MIT license. This
gem depends on it; it is not part of this gem.
